# Once Upon a Time: "If this spell is the first spell you've cast this game" - only spells Bot1 has cast count. Bot2's
# Lightning Bolt on turn 2 is not one of them, so Bot1 casts Once Upon a Time without paying its cost in response (no
# mana at all; the Bolt still resolves for 3). The top five cards of the library are Lightning Bolts: no creature or land
# card among them, so nothing is revealed, nothing is asked and all five go to the bottom, leaving the hand as it was.

[Bot1 Deck]
Once Upon a Time
Island x6
Lightning Bolt x5
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x14

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Once Upon a Time.Cast(Ability: Without)
! Bot1.Arrange
! Bot1.Choose
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Once Upon a Time
Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
Bot1.Library.Count = 15
